{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2148-08-05 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, Mr. ___. I'm Dr. ___, part of your hospital team. You're here today for stem cell mobilization with high-dose Cytoxan as part of your multiple myeloma treatment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2148-08-05 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. I’ve been looking forward to getting this done. Everything’s been delayed a bit."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2148-08-05 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. I see you had some concerns about swelling in your legs recently and a 28-pound weight gain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2148-08-05 14:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, the swelling came on suddenly. I wasn’t sure if it was my heart or something else."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2148-08-05 14:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news — your echo showed normal heart function, and your cardiologist cleared you. But we did notice something when we placed a catheter earlier."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2148-08-05 14:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh? What was that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2148-08-05 14:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We drained about two liters of urine. That suggests significant urinary retention, likely contributing to the leg swelling."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2148-08-05 14:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, I didn’t realize it was that much. I do have trouble emptying sometimes with my neo-bladder."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2148-08-05 14:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. You mentioned you’re supposed to do straight cathing daily, but haven’t been doing it regularly?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2148-08-05 14:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I try, but sometimes I skip it. And I’ve had mucus plugging before — urology helped with that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2148-08-05 14:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We recommend you restart daily cathing to prevent this from happening again. If it continues, we’ll get urology involved again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2148-08-05 14:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll be more consistent. So can we still do the chemotherapy today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2148-08-05 14:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Your urine test on admission was clean, no infection. So we’re going ahead with Cytoxan as planned."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2148-08-05 14:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. Will I need any special prep?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2148-08-05 14:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve already started — you got a fluid bolus and are on IV fluids. We also gave MESNA to protect your bladder, and will continue it every three hours."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2148-08-05 14:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember that from last time. It’s important because of my neo-bladder, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2148-08-05 14:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’re being extra careful. You’re also on your usual medications — Advair, Spiriva, citalopram, and hydrochlorothiazide."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2148-08-05 14:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I stopped Coumadin a week ago — for the transplant, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2148-08-05 14:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Your INR was normal on admission, so it’s safe to hold it temporarily. The risk of bleeding from low platelets outweighs the stroke risk short-term."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2148-08-05 14:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. I was a little worried about that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2148-08-06 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2148-08-06 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m okay. A little tired, but no nausea or pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2148-08-06 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s good. We’re continuing your IV fluids and monitoring your urine output closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2148-08-06 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "The swelling in my legs is already a bit better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2148-08-06 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that’s expected now that we’ve relieved the retention. We’ve also started a lower dose of hydrochlorothiazide to help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2148-08-07 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. We have some updates. Last night, your temperature went up to 100.3, and you had some diarrhea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2148-08-07 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, just once or twice. I feel fine now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2148-08-07 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked a chest X-ray — it was clear. No signs of infection. Stool test came back negative for C. diff."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2148-08-07 08:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it was probably just a small reaction to the chemo?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2148-08-07 08:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Very likely. We’re keeping you one more day for observation, but you’re doing well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2148-08-07 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I saw the X-ray report mentioned a clavicle fracture. Is that new?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2148-08-07 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s not new — it’s listed as possibly pathologic due to your myeloma, but unchanged from before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2148-08-07 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should I be worried about that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2148-08-07 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not right now. Your oncologist will review your recent MRI findings, which showed some spinal changes, but no cord compression."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2148-08-07 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember that — they weren’t sure if it was tumor or a fracture."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2148-08-07 10:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Correct. But your bone marrow biopsy shows less than 5% plasma cells — that’s excellent progress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2148-08-07 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All your cultures came back negative — blood, urine, stool. No infection detected."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2148-08-07 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. So I can go home tomorrow?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2148-08-07 15:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We’ll discharge you tomorrow morning. You’ll take ciprofloxacin for infection prevention, and continue acyclovir for shingles prophylaxis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2148-08-07 15:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the Coumadin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2148-08-07 15:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Do not restart it. Your hematologist will guide when or if to resume, likely after your transplant."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2148-08-07 15:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And I should keep doing the daily cathing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2148-08-07 15:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, very important. Call urology if you have mucus issues or can’t empty well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2148-08-08 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news — you’re cleared to go home. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2148-08-08 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Much better. Ready to get back to normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2148-08-08 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll need to watch for fever, shortness of breath, chest pain, or bleeding. If any of those happen, call your doctor or go to the ER."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2148-08-08 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And I have my follow-up appointments scheduled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2148-08-08 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Keep taking your medications as listed, especially the ciprofloxacin for 10 days. Use Ativan only if you have nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2148-08-08 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, doctor. I appreciate all the care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2148-08-08 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. You did well. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2148-08-05 13:49:00",
    "admission_end": "2148-08-08 12:30:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "Mr. ___ was admitted for high-dose Cytoxan as part of stem cell mobilization for multiple myeloma. He had developed new bilateral leg edema and a 28-pound weight gain, which was attributed to urinary retention due to inadequate self-catheterization of his neo-bladder, draining 2 liters upon Foley placement. Chemotherapy proceeded as planned after confirmation of no active infection. He spiked a low-grade fever and had transient diarrhea, but cultures were negative and symptoms resolved. He was monitored for cardiac and pulmonary risks, both of which were stable. He was discharged home in stable condition with instructions to continue daily catheterization, take ciprofloxacin prophylaxis, and follow up with his oncology and urology teams.",
    "problems": [
      "Encounter for antineoplastic chemotherapy",
      "Urinary complications, not elsewhere classified",
      "Chronic airway obstruction, not elsewhere classified",
      "Multiple myeloma, without mention of having achieved remission",
      "Retention of urine, unspecified",
      "Herpes zoster without mention of complication",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Atrial fibrillation",
      "Abdominal aneurysm without mention of rupture",
      "Personal history of malignant neoplasm of bladder"
    ]
  }
}
